# Mira Design Language

Vibe: pure, soft, warm, reassuring, low-anxiety.

## Colors

| Token | Hex | Usage |
|-------|-----|-------|
| pearl | #FBF7F2 | Primary background |
| warm-white | #FFFDF9 | Card/surface background |
| soft-tan | #EFE3D4 | Elevated surface |
| tan | #E8D9C5 | Border, subtle surface |
| terracotta | #D98E5A | Primary accent |
| terracotta-dark | #C97B5A | Accent hover/active |
| warm-brown | #4A3F35 | Body text |
| sage | #8DA888 | Urgency: low |
| amber | #E0A458 | Urgency: medium |
| coral-red | #C56B5C | Urgency: emergency |

## Typography

- Headings: rounded display serif (e.g. Fraunces, DM Serif Display) -- subject to change
- Body: clean rounded sans (e.g. Nunito) -- subject to change
- Large, friendly, readable sizing.

## Layout

- Responsive design: UI adapts to both mobile and desktop screen sizes.
- 16-24px rounded corners on cards, buttons, inputs.
- Soft diffuse shadows, generous spacing.
- Large tap targets (minimum 44px) for touch-friendly interaction.
- Gentle transitions between screens/states.

## Tone

- Microcopy must be warm, human, and reassuring throughout.
- No clinical jargon in patient-facing text.
- No alarming language; use "contact your maternity team" not "seek immediate medical attention" (except for 999 emergencies).
